.TH auto-group-check 8

\" auto-man2man (used in generating subcommand lists) depends on this section
.SH NAME
.PP
auto-group-check - Verify that owner of a process is a member of group

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-group-check group caller
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
group   Group that the process owner must belong to
caller  Name of the calling program, usually $0 in a script
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-group-check
command verifies that the user who owns the calling process is
a member of the specified group.  If not, an error is printed
including "caller", the name of the calling program, which is
usually specified at "$0" in a script.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-group-check operator $0
.ad
.fi

.SH FILES
.nf
.na
/etc/group, /etc/passwd
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-admin(8), auto-root-check(8)

